              "text": "Because **\"Glenwood Pool\"** is a common name, you might be looking for one of several prominent pools and aquatic resorts across the United States. \n\nThe most well-known locations are listed below, categorized by their location:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Glenwood Hot Springs Pool (Glenwood Springs, Colorado)\nThis is the most famous \"Glenwood Pool\" and is recognized as the **world's largest mineral hot springs pool**. It has been a historic therapeutic and recreational destination since 1888.\n* **The Grand Pool:** Spanning over two city blocks, this massive pool contains over a million gallons of water and is kept at a comfortable 90\u00b0F to 94\u00b0F (32\u00b0C to 34\u00b0C). It features lap lanes and a diving area.\n* **The Therapy Pool:** A warmer pool kept at approximately 104\u00b0F (40\u00b0C) for soothing relaxation.\n* **Yampah Mineral Baths:** A collection of five natural hot spring pools featuring varying temperatures, cold plunges, and a serene, adult-oriented layout.\n* **Sopris Splash Zone:** A family-friendly area that includes water slides, a splash pad, and a fast-moving adventure river.\n* **Access:** Requires a daily admission pass (pricing varies by season and age, generally starting around $30 to $50+).\n\n### 2. Glenwood Pool & Recreation Club (Silver Spring / Forest Glen, Maryland)\nA historic, non-profit, member-run community swim club established in 1953. It is tucked into a quiet, wooded setting along a creek in the historic Forest Glen neighborhood.\n* **Features:** A state-of-the-art, L-shaped 25-meter pool (which allows lap swimming even during recreational hours), a 13-foot deep diving well with two diving boards, a zero-depth beach entry, a separate fenced baby pool, and a \"tea cup\" water fountain. \n* **Community:** It hosts local competitive swim and dive teams (the Glenwood Tigers).\n* **Access:** Private membership-based. Due to its popularity, there is a notoriously long waitlist of several years to join.\n\n### 3. Glenwood Pool / Community Center (Columbus, Ohio)\nA public municipal pool operated by the Columbus Recreation and Parks Department, located in the Greater Hilltop community at 1888 Fairmont Ave.\n* **The Facility:** The entire pool underwent a massive redesign and celebrated its grand reopening in July 2023. The modern facility features a 6-lane (25-yard) lap pool, a diving pool with 1-meter boards, an activity pool with a zero-depth entry, a wading pool, water slides, and a plunge pool.\n* **Access:** Open to the public during the summer season. Admission requires a Columbus Recreation and Parks \"Leisure Card\" (which is free to obtain at any local community center) plus a small daily entry or season pass fee.\n\n### 4. Other Notable Mentions:\n* **Glennwood Pool (Evans, Georgia):** A neighborhood junior-Olympic-sized outdoor community pool that offers seasonal memberships to residents and non-residents.\n* **Glenwood Park Pool (Atlanta, Georgia):** A private, resident-focused 6-lane junior-Olympic saline pool that includes a fitness center, picnic tables, and a kids' water play area.\n\n***\n\n*If you are looking for specific information (like current hours, admission prices, or swim lessons) for one of these pools, please reply with the city or state you are located in!*",
